{"name":"Burro","hex":"#947764","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"burro","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small donkey, especially when used as a pack animal or one that is feral and lives in the southwestern United States or northern Mexico."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/burro"}],"entries":[{"title":"Donkey","blocks":[{"text":"The donkey or ass is a domesticated equine. It derives from the African wild ass, Equus africanus, and may be classified either as a subspecies thereof, Equus africanus asinus, or as a separate species, Equus asinus. It was domesticated in Africa some 5000–7000 years ago, and has been used mainly as a working animal since that time."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Donkey_in_Clovelly%2C_North_Devon%2C_England.jpg/330px-Donkey_in_Clovelly%2C_North_Devon%2C_England.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donkey","wikidata":"Q19707"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Panehsi_001.jpg/500px-Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Panehsi_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Panehsi_001.jpg/1280px-Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Panehsi_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Panehsi_001.jpg/500px-Maler_der_Grabkammer_des_Panehsi_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Donkey in an Egyptian painting c. 1298–1235 BC","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaler_der_Grabkammer_des_Panehsi_001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Baudet.jpg/500px-Baudet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parse